    {
      "id": "troubleshooting#8",
      "docId": "troubleshooting",
      "title": "Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "The connection drops during a long conversation",
      "text": "Sessions are capped so a forgotten tab cannot hold a realtime connection open indefinitely. The app\nwarns before the limit and then ends cleanly. It mints a fresh credential and replays the recent\nconversation, so you can carry on where you left off. If it drops well before the limit, the network is dropping the WebRTC connection. This happens on\nnetworks that block UDP; the fallback to WebSocket is automatic, though it will restart the audio\npath.",
